Package: t1bridge-ubuntu
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, dkms, systemd (>= 256), iio-sensor-proxy
Suggests: libfprint-2-2 (>= 1:1.95.1+tod1-0ubuntu2+t1bridge1), fprintd (>= 1.94.5-4+t1bridge1)
Description: Apple T1 iBridge support (T1Bridge) for Ubuntu
 Touch Bar display, Touch ID authentication broker, private T1 network link
 and xART storage for MacBook Pros with an Apple T1 chip, from
 standardagents/t1bridge, with DKMS kernel modules (T1 configuration
 selector, Touch Bar DRM, NCM link, sleep/wake notification).
 .
 Installing this package takes over the T1 at the next boot: the T1 comes up
 in USB configuration 2 and the legacy apple-ibridge Touch Bar driver is
 blocked. Use t1-switch.sh from t1bridge-ubuntu to install it, because that
 also keeps the login and lock screens off the fingerprint reader and can
 revert. Fingerprint use needs the matching +t1bridge libfprint and fprintd
 packages.
